┌─ API examples ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                            │
│  To compile and link the programs against `libbic.a` given it is already   │
│  compiled, type `make $TARGET`, where $TARGET is the path of a file below  │
│  excluding the `.c` suffix. Of course, BACKEND and INTWIDTH must also be   │
│  preserved from the original `libbic.a` compilation.                       │
│                                                                            │
│  Executing a program without passing any flags will show the available     │
│  options.                                                                  │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/cache-access.c`: a program to visualize the cache access patterns  │
│    of the different cache types. It runs the ranking and unranking         │
│    algorithms and counts how many times each cache entry is accessed.      │
│    Then, it prints a heatmap of the cache accesses.                        │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/cache-size.c`: a program to measure the memory savings of the      │
│    different cache types compared to their full counterparts. It prints    │
│    the percentage of memory save for various parameter configurations and  │
│    standard deviation levels.                                              │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/cache-sparse-size.c`: a program to compare dense vs sparse cache   │
│    sizes for RBO/boustrophedonic orders. Demonstrates the halving set      │
│    column optimization savings for `comb`, `acc`, and `scomb` caches.      │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/cli.c`: a simple CLI to test the available algorithms. It will     │
│    unrank a random integer to a composition and rank it back, showing      │
│    performance stats and other information.                                │
│    The rank and unrank algorithms can be selected independently.           │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/enum.c`: a program to enumerate all possible compositions for a    │
│    given `n`, `k`, and `d`.                                                │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/perf.c`: a program to measure the performance of the different     │
│    (un)ranking algorithms, orders, and cache types. It iterates through a  │
│    range of `k` values and measures the CPU cycles for each combination.   │
│    The output is a table that can be used to compare the performance of    │
│    the different configurations.                                           │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/ratio-n-kd.c`: a program to benchmark unranking performance as a   │
│    function of n/kd ratio (0.05 to 2.0). Compares all orders at fixed      │
│    k=32, d=255 to show how order performance varies with composition       │
│    density.                                                                │
│                                                                            │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
